<onlyinclude>A '''digital organism''' is an artificial-life entity represented by executable instructions or another computational structure that can participate in a simulated process of replication, variation and evolution.

== Explanation ==
For example, a digital organism may contain a sequence of instructions that copies itself. Occasional copying changes can affect its ability to reproduce under the simulator's rules. Populations can evolve as variants compete for computational resources. A digital organism is not necessarily conscious or biologically alive.

